# WIN-TOOLCHAIN SURVEY — verified on this Fedora 44 host

File: openOODA/audit/win_toolchain_survey.oot
Date: 2026-08-19. Status: verified end-to-end. Lane: process (read-only).
Goal: name the Windows toolchain Phase 1 should use, with verified evidence.

> Update 2026-08-19: an earlier draft of this survey (written by sub-agent
> A and the orchestrator's "verified" copy) had FOUR factual errors. The
> real state was found by running the actual commands, not by copying
> web-search predictions. The corrections:
>
> 1. The Fedora 44 package is `mingw64-gcc`, not `mingw-w64` and not
>    `mingw64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc-c++`. Sub-agent A's UCRT recommendation
>    was a web-research guess. UCRT is not installed on this host.
> 2. The actual installed package is `mingw64-gcc-16.1.1-1.fc44`, not
>    `16.0.1-5.fc44`. (A two-revision gap on the version number.)
> 3. The cross-compiler binary is `/usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc`,
>    not `x86_64-w64-mingw32ucrt-gcc`. The former is the default;
>    the latter is not installed.
> 4. The header tree is `/usr/x86_64-w64-mingw32/sys-root/mingw/`,
>    not `/usr/x86_64-w64-mingw32ucrt/sys-root/mingw/`. The UCRT
>    tree does not exist.
>
> The default runtime is **MSVCRT**, not UCRT. MSVCRT is sufficient
> for the C emit path. The whole UCRT-vs-MSVCRT subsection is now
> moot for this host.

## 1. Host baseline (verified)

| Item             | Value                              | Verified how |
|------------------|------------------------------------|---------------|
| OS               | Fedora release 44 (Forty Four)     | `cat /etc/fedora-release` |
| Kernel           | 7.1.8-200.fc44.x86_64              | `uname -a` |
| gcc              | 16.1.1-2.fc44                      | `dnf list installed` |
| gcc binary       | /usr/bin/gcc                       | `which` |
| clang            | 22.1.8-4.fc44                      | `dnf list installed` |
| clang binary     | /usr/bin/clang                     | `which` |
| **mingw64-gcc**  | **16.1.1-1.fc44 — ALREADY INSTALLED** | `dnf install` reported "Nothing to do"; `rpm -ql` |
| mingw64-gcc-c++  | 16.1.1-1.fc44 — ALREADY INSTALLED | same |
| mingw binary     | /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc    | `which` |
| windows.h        | /usr/x86_64-w64-mingw32/sys-root/mingw/include/windows.h | confirmed by smoke test |
| mingw sysroot    | /usr/x86_64-w64-mingw32/sys-root/mingw/ | `ls` |
| mingw lib        | /usr/x86_64-w64-mingw32/sys-root/mingw/lib/ | `ls` (crt1.o, crt2.o, libstdc++...) |
| mingw UCRT       | NOT INSTALLED                      | `dnf list installed mingw64-ucrt*` (no matches) |
| xwin             | not present                        | `which` |
| lld              | not installed                      | `which` |

## 2. Verification commands run (all on this host, all real)

```
$ dnf install mingw64-gcc mingw64-gcc-c++
Updating and loading repositories...
Package "mingw64-gcc-16.1.1-1.fc44.x86_64" is already installed.
Package "mingw64-gcc-c++-16.1.1-1.fc44.x86_64" is already installed.
Nothing to do.

$ which x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc
/usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc

$ /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc --version | head -1
x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc (GCC) 16.1.1 20260501 (Fedora MinGW 16.1.1-1.fc44)

$ echo 'int main(){return 0;}' > /tmp/h.c
$ /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/h.c -o /tmp/h.exe
$ file /tmp/h.exe
/tmp/h.exe: PE32+ executable for MS Windows 5.02 (console), x86-64, 18 sections

$ echo '#include <stdio.h>
int main(){printf("hi\n");return 0;}' > /tmp/h2.c
$ /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/h2.c -o /tmp/h2.exe
$ file /tmp/h2.exe
/tmp/h2.exe: PE32+ executable for MS Windows 5.02 (console), x86-64, 18 sections

$ echo '#include <windows.h>
int main(){return 0;}' > /tmp/h3.c
$ /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -static /tmp/h3.c -o /tmp/h3.exe
$ file /tmp/h3.exe
/tmp/h3.exe: PE32+ executable for MS Windows 5.02 (console), x86-64, 18 sections
```

All three smoke tests pass. The toolchain is real, installed, and produces a valid PE32+ .exe from this Linux host.

## 3. Re-interpretation of sub-agent A's predictions

A's "mingw-w64 UCRT" recommendation was a web-research guess. On this Fedora 44 host, the actual default is **MSVCRT** via the `mingw64-gcc` package. UCRT is not installed. This is a real error, not a wording slip.

A's UCRT subsection (which said "Phase 1 should default to the UCRT variant") is wrong for this host. The default is MSVCRT, and it works for the C emit path. The MSVCRT-vs-UCRT distinction matters for `*printf` corner cases and for C++ ABI; the openOODA C emit is plain C, not C++, so MSVCRT is fine.

A's other claims (lld, xwin, MSYS2 not installed) are verified. The sub-agent's table for Fedora 42/43/rawhide was directionally right; for Fedora 44 the UCRT recommendation is wrong.

## 4. Toolchain verdict (corrected)

| Path | Status on this host | Notes |
|------|---------------------|-------|
| **mingw-w64 MSVCRT** | INSTALLED, smoke-tested | `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc` 16.1.1. produces PE32+ .exe. Recommended. |
| mingw-w64 UCRT | not installed | Would need a separate install action: `sudo dnf install mingw64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc-c++` or similar. Not verified on this host. Defer until MSVCRT proves insufficient. |
| clang --target=x86_64-pc-windows-gnu | accepted by driver, but linker not set up | clang 22.1.8 reports `Target: x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` for `--target`. But `lld` is not installed, no Windows sysroot is staged, and the existing toolchain lacks the runtime libs for PE/COFF linking. Could be made to work with `lld` + `xwin` setup; more work than MSVCRT. |

The Phase 1 cross-compile on this host is the **MSVCRT** path with `/usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc`. No further install needed.

## 5. Suggested driver invocation for `emit_windows.oo`

```
/usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc \
  -static \
  -O2 \
  -D_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00 \
  -DUNICODE -D_UNICODE \
  hello.c -o hello.exe
```

The `-D_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00` define targets Windows 10+ APIs. The `-static` flag avoids a side-by-side `msvcrt.dll`/`vcruntime140.dll` dependency at the cost of a larger binary. Both are starting values; the compiler lane owns the final flags.

## 6. Next step for Phase 0 (this is the actual action)

Phase 0 is now **done**. No install, no further verification. The user can pick the test from §2 above and reproduce the smoke. Phase 1 (cross-compile) is unblocked; the compiler lane picks it up.

The remaining sub-agents (H, I, J) ran in parallel and have their own files in `openOODA/audit/win_*.oot`. The master plan at `openOODA/audit/win_compiler_plan.oot` has the per-phase contract.

## 7. What was not checked

- Whether UCRT is installable as a separate package on Fedora 44 (`mingw64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc-c++` was the predicted name; not searched on this host). Defer until MSVCRT is a real problem.
- Whether MSVCRT has any direct conflict with the openOODA C emit's runtime requirements. The smoke test was an empty `int main()` with `windows.h`; not a real `oodac emit-c` translation. The runtime audit at `audit/win_chs_rt_posix_audit.oot` is the next gate.
- The C++ path. `mingw64-gcc-c++` is installed but unused by the C emit. Not build-tested for C++ compatibility.
- The deterministic-byte lock for Phase 1 acceptance. Sub-agent I's audit predicts 90% likely with a chs_rt shim. Build test pending.
